  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA cold front will push across the area Thursday and Thursday\nnight. Low-level moisture pooling ahead of the boundary will \npush surface dewpoints back into the 60s to lower 70s supporting\ndecent surface-based instability. Meso Nam showing effective\nlayer CAPES over 2000 for much of the area with most unstable \nCAPES over 3000. Deep layer vertical shear of 25 to 40 KTs will\nbe sufficient for updraft storm organization. Meso Nam showing \nDCAPE values of 1000 to 1300. Given a dry mid-level layer and \nsteepening lapse rates, downdraft momentum transport and hail \nsurvival will be enhanced, supporting a threat for localized \ndamaging wind gusts and hail.",
